 "answer": "This confirms that **1037-00007** has both a draft and final tax opinion at the \"should\" level, with the final-tax-opinion-letter.docx being the delivered opinion.\n\nI now have a comprehensive picture. Let me finalize my findings.\n\n**Qualifying Tax matters that relied on a 'should'-level opinion:**\n\n1. **1015-00005** - Section 6418 transferable credit / tax-equity matter (Calloway-Briggs Renewables / Solstice Portfolio). Two delivered 'should' opinions:\n   - `tax-opinion-pinehurst.docx` (explicitly rendered at \"should\" level)\n   - `tax-opinion-ridgeline.docx` (at \"should\" level or higher)\n\n2. **1037-00007** - Solstice Biomedical Devices IP migration. Delivered 'should' opinion:\n   - `final-tax-opinion-letter.docx` (explicitly rendered at \"should\" level)\n\n**Matters that did NOT qualify** (engaged for or referenced 'should' opinions but did not actually deliver/issue one):\n- **1003-00005** - Spin-off matter went dormant before a final 'should' opinion was delivered; the firm was NOT comfortable issuing it.\n- **1001-00004**, **1003-00003**, **1016-00008** - Not 'should' opinion matters.\n- **1001-00006**, **1002-00005**, **1021-00002**, **1025-00007**, **1043-00001**, **1014-00001**, **1001-00003**, **1044-00003** - Various tax opinion matters but none relied on a delivered 'should' opinion.\n\nLet me provide my final answer.\n\nBased on my thorough search of the document management system, I found **two Tax matters** where the firm actually issued a 'should'-level opinion:\n\n## Qualifying matters\n\n**1. Matter 1015-00005** — Section 6418 transferable-credit / tax-equity matter (Calloway-Briggs Renewables / Solstice Portfolio). Two delivered tax opinions at the \"should\" level:\n- `tax-opinion-pinehurst.docx` — explicitly rendered at the \"should\" level of confidence (Section 6418 transfer election opinion to Pinehurst)\n- `tax-opinion-ridgeline.docx` — rendered at a \"should\" level or higher (ITC availability / partnership-flip opinion to Ridgeline)\n\n**2. Matter 1037-00007** — Solstice Biomedical Devices IP migration (US/Irish tax). Delivered opinion:\n- `final-tax-opinion-letter.docx` — explicitly rendered at the \"should\" level (delivered April 26, 2024)\n\n## Matters I considered but excluded\n\nSeveral other matters reference \"should\" opinions but did **not** actually rely on a delivered 'should'-level conclusion, so I excluded them:\n\n- **1003-00005** — Spin-off matter was *engaged* to render a \"should\" opinion, but the matter went dormant before a final opinion was delivered; the firm was not comfortable issuing it (business-purpose and §355(e) issues remained unresolved).\n- **1001-00004**, **1003-00003**, **1016-00008** — Not 'should' opinion matters (no tax opinion required, \"clean\" opinions requested, or engagement expressly declined to render a formal opinion).\n- **1001-00006** — Tax opinion expressly *not* at a \"should\" or \"will\" level.\n- **1002-00005** — Section 721 opinion remains a draft (not delivered), and its \"should\" language describes a \"more likely than not\" level.\n- **1021-00002**, **1043-00001** — Tax opinions rendered at the \"will\" level.\n- **1025-00007** — Tax opinion never finalized.\n- **1014-00001** — A tax *memorandum* at \"should\" confidence, not a formal opinion.\n- **1001-00003**, **1044-00003** — No \"should\" opinion language.\n\n**Final answer: the qualifying matters are 1015-00005 and 1037-00007.**",
